course: dictionary
lesson: 15886
title: Unintentional
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Unintentional means not done on purpose. The prefix un- means not, and intention means a plan or aim to do something. So an unintentional push is a push you did not plan to make. «Sam knocked the cup off the table with his elbow. It was an unintentional push.» He did not mean to do it.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «Mia's comment was an unintentional insult; she did not mean to hurt Ben.» The words did not mean to hurt tell you the insult was an accident. Ask yourself: did the person mean to do it? If not, the word is probably unintentional.
explain: Saying sorry still matters, even when something was unintentional. «I unintentionally broke the window with my football, so I told Mum straight away.» Accidents can still hurt people, so we say sorry and try to put things right.
fact: Unintentional means not done on purpose; accidental.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unintentional means not intentional.
fact: «Unintentionally» is the adverb: it tells you how something was done, as in «She unintentionally knocked over the jug».
fact: Phrases you will meet are «completely unintentional» and «unintentional mistake».
fact: In law, unintentional harm is treated differently from harm done on purpose, which is why people ask, «Did you mean to do it?»
exercise: What does unintentional mean? | Done many times | Done with a big smile | *Not done on purpose | Done very carefully, step by step
exercise: Which word means the same as accidental? | *Unintentional | Careful | Deliberate | Planned
exercise: Maya says sorry after she unintentionally bumps Lily. Why is saying sorry still important? | *It shows you care, even when the harm was not on purpose | It only matters for adults | It is never needed after an accident | It makes the other person pay
test: Which phrase means a mistake that was not planned? | careful choice | *unintentional mistake | planned surprise | deliberate trick
test: Which word is the adverb in «He unintentionally broke the cup»? | *unintentionally | cup | slowly | broke
exam: Read: «Ella's joke was unintentionally rude, so she apologised.» What does unintentionally suggest? | Planned for weeks | Shouted loudly | *Not done on purpose | Done with great skill
